          <change when="2011-08-23T17:18:10.996-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/simoeis">Vote - AcceptText - This is a good suggestion.  It would be nice if proposals like this were supported by a handful (no exhaustive list) of specific parallels, no matter how common the formula might be.  The original editor dotted the tau in "kata."  Any chance that the traces actually belong to theta?  There's apparently no photograph available online or in print that one could check.</change>
          <change when="2011-08-23T17:18:10.984-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/joshuad.sosin">Vote - AcceptText - A nice emendation. Recommend accept. Syntax should (a) attribute the correction and (b) indicate the regularization, as follows: &amp;lt;:&amp;lt;:[κα]θὰ|reg|[κα]τ̣ὰ:&amp;gt; γέγραπται|SoSOL:G. Claytor|[κα]τ̣αγέγραπται:&amp;gt;; finalizer clean up regs throughout.</change>
          <change when="2011-08-12T15:58:41.034-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">In l.4, separated the editor's κα]ταγέγραπται to κα]τὰ γέγραπται and added reg κα]θὰ. This part of the normal clause in contracts: ἐὰν δὲ μὴ ἀποδῶι (or another verb) καθὰ γέγραπται ἀποτεισάτω κτλ.</change>
